/1. Shri Y.B. Chavan, to be Deputy Prime Minister
 and Cabinet Minister in charge of the Ministry of
 Home Affairs;

/2. Shri H.N. Bahuguna, to be Cabinet Minister in
 charge of the Ministry of Finance;

/3. Shri Brahm Parkash, to be Cabinet Minister in
 charge of the Ministry of Agriculture & Irrigation;

/4. Shri Hitendra Desai, to be Cabinet Minister in
 charge of the Ministry of Commerce & Civil
 Supplies;

/5. Shri Purushottam Kaushik, to be Cabinet Minister
 in charge of the Ministry of Information and
 Broadcasting;

/6. Shri Ram Kinkar, to be Cabinet Minister in charge
 of the Ministry of Works, Housing, Supply and
 Rehabilitation;

/7. Shri H.R. Khanna, to be Cabinet Minister in
 charge of the Ministry of Law, Justice & Company
 Affairs;

/8. Shri S.N. Mishra, to be Cabinet Minister in
 charge of the Ministry of External Affairs;

/9. Shri K.C. Pant, to be Cabinet Minister in charge
 of the Ministry of Energy;

/10. Shri T.A. Pai, to be Cabinet Minister in charge
 of the Ministry of Petroleum, Chemicals and
 Fertilizers; also, for the present, to be in
 charge of the Ministry of Railway;

/11. Shri Biju Patnaik, to be Cabinet Minister in
 charge of the Ministry of Steel, Mines & Coal;

/12. Shri Mohamed Shafi Quresani, to be Cabinet Minister
 in charge of the Ministry of Labour;

/13. Shri Rabi Ray, to be Cabinet Minister in charge
 of the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare;

/14. Shri K. Brahmananda Reddi, to be Cabinet Minister
 in charge of the Ministry of Industry;

P.K.T.
500 Copies.
 ...2/-
